\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0   See, Jesus lives with His people
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 He is conversing with them
\par His problems and that of His fear,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par None of them ever feels it.
\par He was frightened, but not gave up.
\par His love was in abundant
\par By that He was victorious.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  A kind of desire so strong
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 That Jesus laid for my sins,
\par The signals of the pass over,
\par That was for His atonement.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Remembered in His communion
\par  His death has made atonement
\par  And that has made us Holy.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. In darkness they made all those plans
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 The Son of God for Jesus
\par Regardless of the strength of death
\par His pow'r, they were not afraid.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Salvation of mankind His aim.
\par This strengthen all of His lambs
\par Because they were not guilty.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4.  It's a form of  bread and of wine
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0  He gave to us His body
\par  And the blood that was so Holy
\par  For mankind to eat and drink.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  His words tells us to eat this food
\par  And in remembrance of Him
\par  That will give eternal life.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  5.   I will bless the Lord my Saviour
\par \pard\li405\sl190\slmult0  You have called me by your grace
\par  Then I should come to your table
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6  Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par To receive and eat your food
\par  I am your own; you are my own
\par  And nothing can on this earth
\par  Separate us from each other.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li405\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.  Someday to come I shall have joy
\par \pard\li405\sl190\slmult0  In heaven the home of peace
\par  In presence of my Saviour Lord
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6  Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par The lamb of God that was slain
\par  I'll give praise to His love always
\par  With echoes of loud voices
\par \pard        Shall sing sweet songs unto Him.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

